---
import Chapter from "../components/Chapter.astro";
import BsnRecordWalkthrough from "../components/BsnRecordWalkthrough.astro";
---

<Chapter id="packets">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <h2>Message formats</h2>
    <p>Read each diagram from left to right. Each size is a wire size. A dashed
    edge identifies a conditional field or a schema-sized field.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="message-format-groups">
    <details class="reference-group message-format-group" id="bgs-packet" open>
      <summary><span><b>Front</b></span></summary>
      <div class="reference-body message-format-body">
        <article>
          <figure class="packet-figure">
            <div class="packet-diagram-scroll">
              <div class="packet-strip bgs-strip" aria-label="Front RPC message: two-byte header length, protobuf header, and optional protobuf body">
                <div class="packet-field field-length"><b>2 bytes</b><span>header length</span><code>uint16 BE</code></div>
                <div class="packet-field field-header"><b>header_length bytes</b><span>RPC header</span><code>protobuf</code></div>
                <div class="packet-field field-body"><b>remaining bytes</b><span>RPC body</span><code>protobuf · can be empty</code></div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <figcaption>One WebSocket binary message.</figcaption>
          </figure>

          <ol class="packet-notes">
            <li><b>The 2-byte prefix gives the RPC header size.</b> Its value equals the
            number of protobuf-header bytes.</li>
            <li><b>The WebSocket message sets the frame boundary.</b> The body ends with
            the WebSocket binary message.</li>
            <li><b>The header routes the call.</b> The service and method select the
            operation. The token identifies the related request.</li>
            <li><b><code>Header.size</code> is optional.</b> If this field is present, its
            value must equal the body size.</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="packet-example"><b>Parser sketch</b><code>read_u16_be → decode Header → decode body from remaining WebSocket bytes</code></p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="reference-group message-format-group" id="bsn-packet" open>
      <summary><span><b>Sunken</b></span></summary>
      <div class="reference-body message-format-body">
        <article>
          <p class="cursor-lede">The route, payload, and padding share <b>one
          continuous bit cursor</b>. The worked example below shows how those
          parts occupy actual bytes.</p>

          <BsnRecordWalkthrough />

          <div class="walkthrough-step">
            <h5>Command responses</h5>
            <span class="step-note">the one record shape with no payload</span>
          </div>
          <p class="cursor-note">A record whose service flag is zero has a fixed
          two-byte form: six command bits, the zero service flag, and a nine-bit
          result. It has no service slot or typed payload.</p>
          <p class="packet-example"><b>Command-response boundary</b><code>6 command + 1 service flag + 9 result = 16 bits</code></p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
</Chapter>
